of 10. 600 possible."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Finland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/41998"} "Pentti Linnosvuo"] " and the USSR’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/44561"} "Makhmud Umarov"] ", world record holder in the Center-Fire Pistol, tied for first in this event. Linnosvuo won the shoot-off, 26-24, to take the gold medal. Linnosvuo would return in 1964 to win the rapid-fire pistol event, becoming only the second shooter, after " [:a {:href "/athletes/44704"} "Al Lane"] " of the USA, to win both of the classic Olympic pistol events. No Finnish flag was available at the range, and one had to be brought in from Melbourne. The medal ceremony was postponed for an hour because of this. Defending champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/44615"} "Joe Benner"] ", was given a lane at the outside of the range, rendering almost nil his chance at retaining the title."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Round 1 Points"] [:th {} "Round 2 Points"] [:th {} "Round 3 Points"] [:th {} "Round 4 Points"] [:th {} "Round 5 Points"] [:th {} "Round 6 Points"] [:th {} "10s"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/41998"} "Pentti Linnosvuo"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "556"] [:td {} "90"] [:td {} "95"] [:td {} "91"] [:td {} "94"] [:td {} "93"] [:td {} "93"] [:td {} "26"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/44561"} "Makhmud Umarov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS